  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\n\nTemperatures are expected to drop down into the 30s and 40s tonight.\nThe greatest likelihood for temperatures in the middle 30s will be in\ncentral Ohio in the cool spots east of Columbus. Went with a frost\nadvisory for Licking, Fairfield, and Hocking counties for tonight.  \n\nThere will also be the potential for some stratus and fog to work\ninto northern portions of the region again tonight with flow off of\nthe lake. Have adjusted cloud cover for tonight across these\nlocations and also have fog in the forecast as well. Have fog mention\nin the HWO as well.\n\nKey Message 2)\n\nA continued dry weather pattern is expected. High temperatures over\nthe next week are expected to be in the 60s and 70s and lows will be\nin the 30s and 40s.",
